.TH WAKU 1 "October 2026" "Waku" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
waku \- native control plane for local coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B waku
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Waku
is a native desktop application for working with local coding agents.
The Debian package includes the provider daemon, JavaScript REPL, and
Computer Use helpers.
.PP
A graphical desktop session and a working Vulkan or OpenGL driver are
required. Native file dialogs use the desktop portal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.waku
User configuration and application state. Removing the Debian package
does not remove this directory.
.SH UPDATES
This package does not enable the tarball self-updater. Install newer
package versions through the system package manager.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dpkg (1)
